{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>He shall not defile himself, a husband among his people.</b> As its Targum: רבא בעמיה — and it is defective (missing) bet, as in בבעל בעמיו. A parallel example: שבי אלמנה בית אביך — and there are many more. Another interpretation: לא יטמא — an ordinary kohen shall not defile himself בבעל בעמיו, that is, through the husband among his people, i.e. through the kohen gadol who is among his people — even though I have permitted you to defile yourself for relatives, you shall not defile yourself for the kohen gadol who is not your relative. Another interpretation: <b>he shall not defile himself as a husband</b> — this refers to the kohen — <b>בעמיו</b>, among his people: not even through other kohanim, apart from those mentioned (as permitted relatives)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The first 'another interpretation' begins with ד״א, rendered as 'Another interpretation'; the second is introduced by ד״א as well, translated without a repeated marker."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:58.993940155Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}